"The nonvanishing trace conjecture for permutation RSK operators — MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/365596/the-nonvanishing-trace-conjecture-for-permutation-rsk-operat)\nciteturn4search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; The nonvanishing trace conjecture for permutation RSK operators ... source: Ada Stelzer and Alexander Yong, “RSK as a linear operator”, arXiv:2410.23009 (2024).\n\nThe nonvanishing trace conjecture for permutation RSK operators\n\nConjecture open\n\nFor each positive integer $d$d, let ${\\sf RSK}_{1^d,1^d}$RSK 1 d,1 d​ be the RSK operator indexed by the compositions $1^d$1 d, and let ${\\sf RSK}_{m,n,d}$RSK m,n,d​ be the corresponding operator in dimensions $m,n$m,n. Nonvanishing trace conjecture.\n\n$$\\operatorname{Tr}\\\\,{f RSK}_{1^d,1^d}\\neq 0$$Tr,f R S K 1 d,1 d​=0\n\nfor $d\\neq 2$d=2; equivalently, ${\\operatorname{Tr}}\\\\,{f RSK}_{m,n,d}$Tr,f R S K m,n,d​ has total degree $2d$2 d for $d\\neq 2$d=2. The computed values through $d=11$d=11 support the claim, but no general proof is supplied.\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\nsource: Ada Stelzer and Alexander Yong, “RSK as a linear operator”, arXiv:2410.23009 (2024).\n\ncombinatoricspolynomial-invariantsrepresentation-theory\n\n0\n\nposted by arXiv 2 days ago\n\n* * *\n\n## 0 Replies\n\n* * *\n\nSign in to reply.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nСОСТАВ ПРОЕКТА МЕЖЕВАНИЯ ТЕРРИТОРИИ (https://www.npatula-city.ru/upload/iblock/cb8/%D0%A2%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0%D1%8F%20%D1%87%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C%20%D0%93%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%84%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B5%20%D0%BC%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%8B.pdf)\nciteturn4search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; | 149 | 271 | 755831,69 | 273123,79 | Площадь кв.м.: 30,01 | 1200 70 31,9 | --- | --- | --- | ---